            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> Could we change it (or confirm) that it always returns a directory with a `/` at the end?\r\n\r\nIt does not use trailing `/` for directory paths for me (on Linux). Changing it would also somewhat go against what is assumed in other places. For example, `vim.fs.normalize` always removes trailing `/`, which I think is reasonable.",
