            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "This check is indeed costly, as it will read the disk each time filetype detection is made (which can be fairly frequent in plugins that rely on `vim.filetype.match()`). And `vim.filetype.match()` is designed to be as fast as possible. At least until there is something like #30086, I'd say this check adds too much overhead.",
            "commit_id": "25286f87c92c3840bda376caf62f067524329905",
            "created_at": "2026-07-02T13:55:22Z",
            "diff_hunk": "@@ -3258,6 +3258,13 @@ function M.match(args)\n \n     local ok_abspath, path = pcall(vim.fs.abspath, name)\n     if ok_abspath then -- First check for the simple case where the full path exists as a key\n+      if name ~= '' then\n+        local stat = vim.uv.fs_stat(path)",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40529#discussion_r3513595663",
