    "comment_regular_data": [
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "OK, so `vim.filetype.match()` should not stat paths on every call (at least for right now) - that makes sense. Also, I do not want this to be blocked by #30086 (not only is it under contentious discussion, but I want dir.lua overriding to be handled relatively quickly, for the sake of mini.files and beyond).\r\n\r\nI reverted to the directory check from `vim.filetype.match()`.\r\n\r\nI moved the check back to the core directory-open path. This keeps the hotpath unchanged while still letting `FileType directory` be the earlier dispatch point for actual directory buffers.\r\n\r\nIf this is not a satisfiable solution I'm seeking advice...",
            "created_at": "2026-07-02T18:46:03Z",
