                "url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth",
                "user_view_type": "public"
            }
        },
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "The `open_buffer` approach is worth considering, but it introduces a new order-of-operations question(s), so it seems preferable to avoid it.\r\n\r\nIt seems to me that if `b_ffname` (aka `nvim_buf_get_name`) [ensures that directory buffers](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40529#discussion_r3512550132) ends with `/`, that has broad long-term value. (And i don't care much that `fnamemodify()` has traditionally removed the trailing slash, though for back-compat that particular function can't be changed)",
            "created_at": "2026-07-02T19:51:27Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40529#issuecomment-4869912330",
            "id": 4869912330,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/40529",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABIkT3Cg",
            "performed_via_github_app": null,
            "reactions": {
                "+1": 0,
                "-1": 0,
                "confused": 0,
                "eyes": 0,
                "heart": 0,
                "hooray": 0,
                "laugh": 0,
                "rocket": 0,
                "total_count": 0,
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/4869912330/reactions"
            },
            "updated_at": "2026-07-02T19:51:27Z",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/4869912330",
            "user": {
                "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/1359421?v=4",
                "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/events{/privacy}",
                "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/followers",
                "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/following{/other_user}",
                "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/gists{/gist_id}",
                "gravatar_id": "",
                "html_url": "https://github.com/justinmk",
                "id": 1359421,
                "login": "justinmk",
                "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjEzNTk0MjE=",
                "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/orgs",
                "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/received_events",
                "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/repos",
                "site_admin": false,
                "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
                "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk/subscriptions",
                "type": "User",
                "url": "https://api.github.com/users/justinmk",
                "user_view_type": "public"
            }
        },
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Can you spare me some more context on the long-term value of this? Generally, it seems like just as often as it's more idiomatic for paths to end in `/` it's more idiomatic for them not to.\r\n\r\nIs the idea here to change the internal and external representation of directories with the invariant of having trailing `/`? So apis like `vim.fs.normalize()` (that echasnovski mentioned earlier) have a trailing `/`? Would this be a breaking change anywhere?\r\n\r\nI do like this idea but seeking a bit of clarification here - AFAIK this change would span a meaty bit of the codebase (not that this makes it any less right, ofc). I think for sure the internal and external representation of directories HAS to match (i.e. have trailing slash or not, one or the other).",
            "created_at": "2026-07-02T21:43:12Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40529#issuecomment-4870711737",
            "id": 4870711737,
            "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/40529",
            "minimized": null,
            "node_id": "IC_kwDOAPphoM8AAAABIlEpuQ",
            "performed_via_github_app": null,
            "reactions": {
                "+1": 0,
                "-1": 0,
                "confused": 0,
                "eyes": 0,
                "heart": 0,
                "hooray": 0,
                "laugh": 0,
                "rocket": 0,
                "total_count": 0,
                "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/4870711737/reactions"
            },
            "updated_at": "2026-07-02T21:44:57Z",
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/neovim/neovim/issues/comments/4870711737",
            "user": {
                "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/62671086?v=4",
                "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/events{/privacy}",
                "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/followers",
                "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/following{/other_user}",
                "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/gists{/gist_id}",
                "gravatar_id": "",
                "html_url": "https://github.com/barrettruth",
                "id": 62671086,
                "login": "barrettruth",
                "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjYyNjcxMDg2",
                "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/orgs",
                "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/received_events",
                "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/repos",
                "site_admin": false,
                "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/starred{/owner}{/repo}",
                "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth/subscriptions",
                "type": "User",
                "url": "https://api.github.com/users/barrettruth",
                "user_view_type": "public"
            }
        },
        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "> it seems like just as often as it's more idiomatic for paths to end in `/` it's more idiomatic for them not to.\r\n\r\nwhen they end with `/` it is useful because it saves an `isdirectory()` check.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n> Is the idea here to change the internal and external representation of directories with the invariant of having trailing `/`? So apis like `vim.fs.normalize()` (that echasnovski mentioned earlier) have a trailing `/`? Would this be a breaking change anywhere?\r\n\r\nit doesn't need to change `vim.fs.normalize()` nor `fnamemodify()` (and they already do work to drop the `/` , so they won't need to adapt either way). \r\n\r\nit only requires a change to `b_ffname` , which will then reflect in `nvim_buf_get_name`. however, if changing `b_ffname` ends up being a huge problem, then we could decide to selectively change `nvim_buf_get_name` . or retreat :)",
            "created_at": "2026-07-02T21:50:14Z",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/40529#issuecomment-4870754997",
